960178	F - Utilities	https://pagrants.fema.gov/#Project/960178/details	1727783	Vanderburgh County	Evansville, City of	The applicant stated that heavy rainfall prior to the incident period resulted in a sinkhole forming underneath the street directly over a sewer line. The applicant noticed a depression in the road and concluded that there was undermining damage beneath the road. The applicant excavated the depression and found a large void beneath the road around a sewage line. The sewage line had burst from the increased water pressure as a result of the heavy rainfall. This lead to undermining around the sewage line and beneath the road. This site was set to be repaired with a new sewage pipe but incident period storms began which raised the water table and prevented the city from completing the repair. After several weeks passed and the water level lowered the city noticed that the original sink hole increased in size and was now putting the entire street in danger. The sink hole continued to expand and eventually damaged a 30-inch water transmission line which had to be repaired in kind but lost 4.5 million gallons of water. Additionally a water diversionary structure sank approximately 2 feet into the earth rendering the structure useless. All of the damages are underneath a FHWA road. 	Site 1 – Sewer Line & Sinkhole (37.96677, -87.57348)	37.96677	-87.57348	4544099	1727783	null	Road, 43.5 CY asphalt/aggregatesurface 82 FT long x 43 FT wide x 4 IN deep pavement collapsed into sinkhole, exposing sewer line
